{"format_version":"vbulletin-3+-thread","url":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/989134-mystery-cult-ish-concept-hench4hire","id":989134,"title":"Mystery cult-ish concept: Hench4Hire","path":["Home","Onyx Path","White Wolf Worlds","Chronicles of Darkness"],"posts":[{"date":"2016-10-17T19:05:31-07:00","id":989134,"title":"Mystery cult-ish concept: Hench4Hire","content":"So, I'm working out the idea of an organization that hires out henchmen to assorted villains (as part of my project to bring as much Venture Bros into ChroD as possible) and I'm thinking of doing them as a mystery cult. They'd work well in a Beast game, due to the crossover potential. In gameplay terms, I think their ability would be something that lets them interact easily with whatever supernatural being is their patron. So a group of henches working for a Promethean would be immune to Disquiet, while a group working for a Mage would be considered Sleepwalkers. To keep it from being unbalanced, I'd have it be that they can only have one boss at a time, and it only applies when they're &quot;on-duty&quot;- in costume and actively working for them.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/5358-geckopirateship","name":"Geckopirateship","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar5358_2.gif","title":"Banned","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Mar 2015"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1383"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-10-17T19:22:20-07:00","id":989142,"title":"","content":"You may want to look at my <a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/mummy-the-curse/875173-example-cult-carnivale\">Carnivale</a>, though they're more Payday Crew than villain henchmen.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>Remi. she/her. game designer.","